      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Sweep any setting\n\nThis is an ordinary text-to-image workflow. Three of its settings are swept at once, with no special sampler: **seed (1-2) x cfg (4, 7, 10) x prompt (2 variants)** = 12 images, saved with the values in their file names, plus one labelled grid per prompt in `output/SweepKit_any_setting/` (and a `sweep_manifest_*.csv` run list).\n\n1. Pick your checkpoint in **Load Checkpoint**.\n2. Queue.\n\n**To sweep another setting:** right-click it on any node and choose **Sweep \"...\"**. SweepKit adds a blue **Sweep Axis** for it and wires it in; edit the values there. The blue **Sweep Plan** turns the axes into one list per setting, and the green **Sweep Collect** gathers your final image into named files and grids."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
